# B0 (no card opened): build the window image tp4-262k8-x-1 from the pushed tp4/262k8-x commit. The profile named is the production default; nothing is baked as the image default (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE).
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists. The image carries every lever module of the merged branches (the sampler kernels, the drafter I/O kernels, the bfloat16 drafter
# switch, prompt_lookup, the V5 split kernels, inert here: no profile of this window sets its flag). No privileged builder container may be up. Never run it during a timing job.
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Duration (estimate): 20-60 min. Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8-x experiments window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8-x and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-x-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8-x commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-x-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
